* Charging infrastructure: *_INFRA_INVCOST are overnight costs in 10'000 EUR2015/MW (Sanvito et al. 2026, arXiv:2602.01862v1, Supplementary Table 3,
* Cost-Base); *_INFRA_COST_OPEX are fixed O&M in 10'000 EUR2015/MW/yr. The model annualises the overnight cost with
* DISCOUNTRATE over EV_INFRA_LIFETIME and retires the infrastructure after it (docs/adr/0038 in the GREAT repo).
* Lifetime: one value for the whole station. Swiss eMobility/EnergieSchweiz (2023), Ladeinfrastruktur in Mietobjekten,
* p. 31, and the HEV/MV paritaetische Lebensdauertabelle (2024): wallbox 8-10 y, basic installation (cabling,
* distribution boards, core drilling) 20-40 y, meters and protection 15 y. With installation being most of the cost,
* the annuity-equivalent single lifetime is about 15-22 y. In 10-year model steps every value from 15 to 24 behaves
* the same: an investment is in place in its own model year and the next one.
SCALAR EV_INFRA_LIFETIME 'Lifetime of EV charging infrastructure (years)' /20/;
